From d464e6a60e15212742665a2edbc4027fdcc3fd85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:08:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(routing): a managed pin on its own endpoint is not an
 override, and a refusal is not a bad sign-in [daveey]

Every turn of an adopted Desktop chat failed before reaching a provider:
"Managed subscription pins cannot override credentials or endpoint", shown as
"The AI service rejected your sign-in", with no Retry.

Why it happened:
- adopt_legacy_session froze the saved endpoint into the launch request, because
  same_route compares the profile's implicit native URL ('') with the saved
  https://api.anthropic.com and calls them different.
- route_runtime passes that launch URL to the resolver as explicit_base_url.
- The managed guard (40f638ec5b) refused any explicit URL, even the pin's own.
- Why it wasn't caught: guard tests used only foreign URLs, and no test ran an
  adopted receipt through a managed route.
- Why it looked like auth: _resolution_failure_reply stamps every resolver failure
  on a local chat auth_permanent, so the card hid the real sentence.

14 of 14 stored receipts carrying a base_url failed before this and resolve after
it. Routing never used that URL, so the guard now refuses only a real override;
auto, custom, other vendors, unknown hosts and any explicit key stay refused.
ModelRoutingError on a local chat reports route_refused on the gateway layer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
